{"title": "Honey Stinger", "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"druid-infobox druid-container noexcerpt\" id=\"druid-container-1\"><div><div class=\"druid-title\">Honey Stinger</div></div><div class=\"druid-section-container\"><div class=\"druid-main-image\"><div class=\"druid-main-images-labels druid-tabs\"><div class=\"druid-main-images-label druid-tab druid-toggleable druid-title-tab focused\" data-druid=\"1-1\" data-druid-tab-key=\"In-Game\">In-Game</div></div><a href=\"/wiki/File:Honey_Stinger.jpg\" class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Honey Stinger.jpg\" src=\"/images/thumb/Honey_Stinger.jpg/250px-Honey_Stinger.jpg?43de34\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"141\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/Honey_Stinger.jpg/375px-Honey_Stinger.jpg?43de34 1.5x, /images/thumb/Honey_Stinger.jpg/500px-Honey_Stinger.jpg?43de34 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div><div class=\"druid-section-container\"><div data-druid-section=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-section druid-section-Information\">Information</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-VariantOf\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-VariantOf\">Variant Of</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-VariantOf druid-data-nonempty\">\nHoarding Bug</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-InternalID\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-InternalID\">Internal ID</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-InternalID druid-data-nonempty\">\nHoneyStinger</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-MaxCount\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-MaxCount\">Max Count</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-MaxCount druid-data-nonempty\">\n10</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-PowerLevel\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-PowerLevel\">Power Level</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-PowerLevel druid-data-nonempty\">\n1</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-CauseofDeath\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-CauseofDeath\">Cause of Death</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-CauseofDeath druid-data-nonempty\">\nMauling</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-IsBodyRecoverable\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-IsBodyRecoverable\">Is Body Recoverable?</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-IsBodyRecoverable druid-data-nonempty\">\nYes</div></div></div><div class=\"druid-section-container\"><div data-druid-section=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-section druid-section-Stats\">Stats</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-Health\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-Health\">Health</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-Health druid-data-nonempty\">\n3</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-Damage\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-Damage\">Damage</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-Damage druid-data-nonempty\">\n30</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-DoorSpeedMultiplier\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-DoorSpeedMultiplier\">Door Speed Multiplier</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-DoorSpeedMultiplier druid-data-nonempty\">\n1.5</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-StunTimeMultiplier\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-StunTimeMultiplier\">Stun Time Multiplier</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-StunTimeMultiplier druid-data-nonempty\">\n0.3</div></div></div></div>\n<p>The <b>Honey Stinger</b> is a hostile or docile entity depending on how players interact with it and is a variant of the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://lethal.miraheze.org/wiki/Hoarding_Bug\">Hoarding Bug</a> added by <b>Wesley's Ememy Variants</b>. It is a large black and brown bee with a stinger, a pair of wings, four longer arms it uses to crawl around, and two shorter arms it uses to grab items.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Mechanics\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Mechanics\">&gt; Mechanics</span></h2>\n<p>While the <b>Honey Stinger</b> behaves very similarly to the Hoarding Bug for its Roaming, Guarding, and Attacking states, the <b>Honey Stinger</b> specifically only attempts to find and collect <b>Bee hives</b>. The <b>Honey Stinger</b> becomes more aggressive and territorial of its nesting area the more hives it collects. If several hives are collected, the <b>Honey Stinger</b> will often attack players it encounters on sight. The <b>Honey Stinger</b> deals 30 damage on contact in its Attacking state.\n</p><p>A <b>Honey stinger treat</b> is randomly available for purchase from the Gift Shop on <a href=\"/wiki/Galetry\" title=\"Galetry\"><b>Galetry</b></a> for \u25ae520. It is not conductive, weighs 21lbs, is two-handed, and is worth \u25ae130. The tooltip mentions that it can be offered to the <b>Honey Stinger</b> as a treat and tribute. If players encounter a <b>Honey Stinger</b>, they can drop the treat on the ground for it to collect. The <b>Honey Stinger</b> will become permanently happy and docile on that save file after collecting it, never attacking players and allowing players to safely take hives they have collected.\n</p><p>However, the tooltip also mentions that the <b>Honey Stinger</b> will remember if players betray it. Players can betray the <b>Honey Stinger</b> by directly attacking it, such as with a shovel. Indirect actions like dropping a conductive item to strike it down with lightning does not count as betrayal. If players do betray the <b>Honey Stinger</b>, it will immediately aggro every time it encounters players on that save file.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Spawn_Chances\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Spawn_Chances\">&gt; Spawn Chances</span></h2>\n<p>The <b>Honey Stinger</b> has a chance to spawn on several moons, most commonly spawning on <a href=\"/wiki/Hyve\" title=\"Hyve\"><b>Hyve</b></a>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"noresize\">\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Moon Name</th>\n<th>Interior or Exterior</th>\n<th>Spawn Chance\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Hyve\" title=\"Hyve\">Hyve</a></td>\n<td>Both</td>\n<td>48.42%, 80.85%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Spine\" title=\"Spine\">Spine</a></td>\n<td>Both</td>\n<td>4.48%, 33.64%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Heap\" title=\"Heap\">Heap</a></td>\n<td>Exterior</td>\n<td>30%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Chasm\" title=\"Chasm\">Chasm</a></td>\n<td>Exterior</td>\n<td>21.84%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Faith\" title=\"Faith\">Faith</a></td>\n<td>Exteiror</td>\n<td>11.01%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Junic\" title=\"Junic\">Junic</a></td>\n<td>Exterior</td>\n<td>10.77%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Crowd\" title=\"Crowd\">Crowd</a></td>\n<td>Exterior</td>\n<td>10%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Infernis\" title=\"Infernis\">Infernis</a></td>\n<td>Interior</td>\n<td>9.85%\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/Alcatras\" title=\"Alcatras\">Alcatras</a></td>\n<td>Exterior</td>\n<td>9.20%\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Bestiary_Entry\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Bestiary_Entry\">&gt; Bestiary Entry</span></h2>\n<table class=\"article-table mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" data-expandtext=\"\u25bc\" data-collapsetext=\"\u25b2\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Honey Stinger<span style=\"padding-left:0.5em;\">&#x2060;</span>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table style=\"border: 15px solid #8E8E83; font-size: 135%; font-family: Tomorrow; color: #01A801; border-spacing: 0px;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"padding: 25px; background-color: #151515;\">HONEY STINGER<br /><br /><br />Sigurd's danger level: 40%<br /><br /><br />Scientific name: Vapir-Mellitera<br /><br /><br />The Honey stinger is a large insect part of the Anthophila, being close to the Melittidae. They tend to inhabit luscious or mountainous areas with the largest colony discovered in the asteroid belt of 56-Vow.<br />The honey stinger has a hard and thick shell on its back to protect itself from any aggressors while the bottom is more soft and vulnerable. It is because of this vulnerability that they prefer to crawl around despite them being excellent at flying.<br /><br /><br />Much like many species of bees they are born from and serve one queen. While the antics of the honey stinger are not extensively studied, it is known that they possess a more playful behaviour than most other families of bees.<br /><br /><br />They take a liking to grabbing and claiming objects they find interesting. Most often these are beehives of smaller species of bees. It is unsure if they understand the concept of a smaller version of themselves existing but it is known that after obtaining several of these hives they become increasingly defensive.<br /><br /><br />While they do not have any aggressive tendencies towards most species they are quick to attack any human who wanders near them, likely due to the frequent exploitation of their hives.<br /><br /><br />It is recommended to stay away from the honey stinger when encountered in the wild. They do not like you but they mean no harm. They are only protective of themselves and their hives.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Audio\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Audio\">&gt; Audio</span></h2>\n<div class=\"noresize\">\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"text-align: center;\" data-expandtext=\"\u25bc\" data-collapsetext=\"\u25b2\">\n<caption style=\"white-space: nowrap;\">Audio\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Action</th>\n<th>Sound\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Walking</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\